ms: prevent port-proxy livelock on stale UDP errors

With IP_RECVERR enabled, recv() or sendto() can consume sk_err
without dequeuing the associated error report. poll() then keeps
reporting POLLERR while normal recvfrom() returns EAGAIN.

The proxy handler previously retried with four 5 us sleeps and
returned MS_OK without draining the queue. This could keep the
SCHED_RR select thread cycling and starve RCU readers and the GP
kthread on a single CPU, leading to an RCU stall panic.

Drain the error queue on EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK and remove the short-sleep
retries. Keep MS_OK for recoverable errors and retain the existing
eight-attempt nonblocking drain budget. Log stale-queue drains once
per 100 occurrences.

Add regression tests where recv() or sendto() consumes sk_err before
the proxy handler runs, and verify that POLLERR clears.

SYNLITE-44184


